# Cargo workspace build output. The default `desktop/target` is used again: the
# `.cargo/config.toml` that used to redirect `build.target-dir` into
# `crates/syncra-sync/target` was removed in F3-A (`docs/DESKTOP-ARCHITECTURE.md` §E.5.2
# ACIK 2) — the single shared workspace `target/` is what actually prevents the OpenSSL
# vendor tree from being compiled twice, so the redirect bought nothing and only made a
# member crate's directory hold the whole workspace's output. Use `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` if a
# shorter path is ever needed (MAX_PATH), not a committed config.
/target

# Stale: `src-tauri` was built standalone (its own `target/`) before `desktop/Cargo.toml`
# made it a workspace member. Left on disk rather than deleted (nothing destructive this
# turn); ignored either way.
/src-tauri/target

# Frontend build output `tauri.conf.json` -> `build.frontendDist` points at (`desktop/dist`),
# produced by `npm run build:desktop`.
/dist

# Tauri-generated JSON schemas for capabilities/ACL editor tooling (`src-tauri/gen/schemas`),
# regenerated by every `cargo check`/`build` — standard Tauri 2 project `.gitignore` entry.
/src-tauri/gen

# npm dependencies of the desktop shell (its own tree, deliberately separate from
# `frontend/node_modules` — `docs/DESKTOP-ARCHITECTURE.md` KARAR A1: `@tauri-apps/*` never
# enters `frontend/package.json`).
/node_modules

# Generated Tauri config overlay (build-time CSP hosts — §E.5.2 ACIK 1). Written by
# `scripts/tauri.mjs` on every `npm run tauri`; never hand-edited, never committed.
/.tauri
